  "question": {
    "text": "A tightly wound solenoid of radius <math><mi>‘</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>’</mi></math> and length <math><mi>‘</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>’</mi></math> has <em>n</em> turns per unit length. It carries an electric current <em>i</em>. Magnetic field at a distance <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> from one of the end (inside the solenoid on its axis) is&nbsp;<math><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math> for <math><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></math> . Then find the value of <em>K</em>.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0097_cfb47849229b.jpg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 103px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
